<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Atropates</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. <a href="/years/331-bce">331</a>–c. 320 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Atropates was a Persian noble who served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrap</a> of Media under the Achaemenid king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-iii">Darius III</a> and fought at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-gaugamela">Gaugamela</a> in 331 BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> later restored him as satrap, and after Alexander's death he made the northern part of Media an independent kingdom, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/media-atropatene">Media Atropatene</a>, named after him. The name lives on in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>.</p></div>
